  "source_text": "Synthetic validation nurse note. No real patient data.\n\nThe driver attends with a current signed GP summary and a three-week measurement log; after reviewing repeated seated measurements, the GP documents that current persistent blood pressure is 178/106 mmHg. The driver recalls a much lower reading after exercise last summer, but that recollection is recorded separately from the current verified log and does not replace its persistent measurements. He denies current chest pain and has not experienced a definite blackout, although he occasionally feels light-headed when getting out of the cab.\n\nDuring today's conversation the driver reports difficulty understanding dispatch when the engine is running, and hearing screening suggests possible hearing loss. No formal audiogram is available. He brought an invoice for a hearing aid consultation rather than a completed test, and neither the better-ear average nor the required frequencies has been measured in the supplied record.\n\nThe driver recently changed his shift pattern and medication schedule, but there is no specialist statement confirming four weeks of control or an assessment of treatment-related symptoms. The nurse distinguishes the verified persistent pressure from those unresolved questions and from the separate hearing complaint.\n",
